odes-twenty-four"],["Rich tea","dish/rich-tea"],["Rose & Crown Pub & Dining Room","dish/rose-crown-pub-dining-room"],["Sausage roll","dish/sausage-roll"],["Scotch egg","dish/scotch-egg"],["Shepherd's pie","dish/shepherd-s-pie"],["Soldiers (food)","dish/soldiers-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/8/8e/Flickr_jspatchwork_146937146--Making_English_muffins_03.jpg","w":500,"h":374,"by":"Jennifer from Columbia, South Carolina, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_jspatchwork_146937146--Making_English_muffins_03.jpg"}},"ingredient/snakehead-fish":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/snakehead-fish","n":"Snakehead (fish)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The snakeheads are members of the freshwater perciform fish family Channidae, native to parts of Africa and Asia. These elongated, predatory fish are distinguished by their long dorsal fins, large mouths, and shiny teeth. They breathe air with gills, which allows them to migrate short distances over land. They have suprabranchial organs, which are primitive forms of labyrinth organs, that develop when they grow older. The two extant genera are Channa in Asia and Parachanna in Africa, consisting of more than 50 species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-snakehead-fish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakehead_(fish)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Khô cá lóc","dish/kho-ca-loc"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Channidae","ingredient/channidae"]]}]},"dish/liangfen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/liangfen","n":"Liangfen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Liangfen, also spelled liang fen, is a Chinese legume dish consisting of starch jelly that is usually served cold, with a savory sauce, often in the summer. It is most popular in northern China, including Beijing, Gansu, and Shaanxi, but may also be found in Sichuan and Qinghai. In Tibet and Nepal it is called laping and is a common street vendor food. In Kyrgyzstan it is an ingredient in a noodle dish called ashlan fu."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-liangfen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liangfen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["A+ Hong Kong Kitchen","dish/a-hong-kong-kitchen"],["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Chinese Tuxedo","dish/chinese-tuxedo"],["Chowking","dish/chowking"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Country Dough","dish/country-dough"],["Cuisine AuntDai","dish/cuisine-auntdai"],["Dandan noodles","dish/da