sine and today it is also popular in Ukraine (as rozsoljnyk) and Belarus (as rasoljnik). A similar dish is common in Poland, where it is known as zupa ogórkowa (literally 'cucumber soup')."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rassolnik"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rassolnik"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Brine","ingredient/brine"],["Kidney","ingredient/kidney"],["Kidneys as food","ingredient/kidneys-as-food"],["Liver as food","ingredient/liver-as-food"],["Pearl barley","ingredient/pearl-barley"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","ref":"site/olgasflavorfactory-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Russian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cabbage soup","dish/cabbage-soup"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kachka (restaurant)","dish/kachka-restaurant"],["Karelian pasty","dish/karelian-pasty"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Khrenovina sauce","dish/khrenovina-sauce"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"],["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"],["Olivier salad","dish/olivier-salad"],["Pancake","dish/pancake